[38;2;124;124;124mLet me think about this carefully.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mWe have two principally polarized abelian varieties (PPAVs) $(A, \lambda_A)$ and[0m[38;2;124;124;124m$(B, \lambda_B)$, where $\lambda_A: A \to A^\vee$ and $\lambda_B: B \to B^\vee$ [0m[38;2;124;124;124mare principal polarizations (isomorphisms).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mAn isogeny $f: A \to B$ that "respects the polarization" means $f^* \lambda_B = [0m[38;2;124;124;124m\lambda_A$, i.e., the pullback of the polarization on $B$ equals the [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mpolarization on $A$. More precisely, $f^\vee \circ \lambda_B \circ f = [0m
